---
title: Filipino Chicken Adobo
servings: 4
time: 45 min
tags: chicken, filipino, dinner, main
cuisine: Filipino
course: main
source: Filipino Chicken Adobo.pdf
---

In a #large nonreactive sauté pan{}, combine @soy sauce{1/4%cup}, @cane vinegar{1/2%cup}(or distilled white vinegar), @garlic{7%cloves}(smashed and peeled), @whole black peppercorns{1%tsp}, and @bay leaves{2}.

Nestle @skin-on bone-in chicken thighs{6} skin-side down into the liquid. Bring to a boil over high heat, then cover and simmer over low heat for ~{20%minutes}.

Turn the chicken over, cover again, and simmer for ~{10%minutes}.

Uncover the pan, increase heat to high, and bring sauce back to a boil. Boil uncovered, basting and turning the chicken occasionally, until the sauce is reduced by half and thickens slightly, about ~{6%minutes}.

Serve hot with @steamed white rice{}.
